  "id": "COMPOUND:22691 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Gama-Mangostin appears to have a complex relationship with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Gama-Mangostin acts as a target for multiple enzymes, including Carboxylesterase 2, which in turn targets specific compounds such as 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and (7E,9E,16Z)-18-hydroxyoctadeca-7,9,16-trien-11,13-diyn-4-one. These compounds are all identified as targets of Gama-Mangostin, and all ultimately lead to the CD276 antigen. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Gama-Mangostin indirectly influences CD276 antigen through the enzymatic activity of Carboxylesterase 2 and the subsequent targeting of specific chemical compounds. The evidence supports a mechanism where Gama-Mangostin's effects are mediated through these intermediates, highlighting a potential pathway involving enzyme-targeted chemical signaling.",
